.TH SWEEF 1 "" "Sweef" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sweef \- independent browser engine in pure Go, with a built-in agent interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sweef gui
.RI [ URL ...]
.br
.B sweef
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sweef is a browser with its own engine, written in Go. It ships as one static
binary with a JavaScript engine and a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server.
This is an alpha release.
.PP
.B sweef gui
starts the graphical browser. The other commands work headless.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui [URL...]
Start the graphical browser.
.TP
.B fetch URL [--html]
Print the page text (or HTML).
.TP
.B snapshot URL [--aria]
Print the accessibility tree of a page.
.TP
.B shot URL [--out FILE]
Render a PNG.
.TP
.B eval URL JS
Evaluate a JavaScript expression after load.
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP server on standard input and output.
.TP
.B serve [--addr ADDR]
Run the JSON-RPC server.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.PP
Run
.B sweef help
for the complete list, including the persistent session commands
(open, click, fill, wait, ...).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/sweef/NOTICE
Third-party attributions.
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/sweefbrowser/sweef/issues
.SH SEE ALSO
